        {
          "id": "thanh-dieu",
          "label": "Thanh điệu (Tones)",
          "exercises": [
            {
              "type": "grammarNote",
              "noNum": true,
              "instructionVi": "",
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "heading",
                  "text": "1. Pitches and Formation",
                  "tone": "purple"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Vietnamese is a tonal language with 6 tones and 5 tone marks."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "There are various ways to translate the name of these tones. The table below combines two approaches; one is the literal translation, and the other is based on the pitches when forming the tone:"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Literal Translation and Pitch Contours of Vietnamese Tones"
                },
                {
                  "type": "table",
                  "columns": [
                    "Vietnamese tone",
                    "Literal translation",
                    "Pitch contour / formation"
                  ],
                  "rows": [
                    [
                      "Thanh ngang",
                      "Level tone",
                      "Mid-level tone"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Thanh sắc",
                      "Sharp tone",
                      "High-rising tone"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Thanh huyền",
                      "Grave tone",
                      "Low-falling tone"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Thanh hỏi",
                      "Question tone",
                      "Low-rising tone"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Thanh ngã",
                      "Tilde tone / Broken tone",
                      "Rising-broken tone"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Thanh nặng",
                      "Heavy tone",
                      "Low-falling or low-dropping tone"
                    ]
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "The diagram below shows the pitch level when forming the tones:"
                },
                {
                  "type": "toneChart",
                  "tones": [
                    {
                      "name": "Ngang",
                      "letter": "a",
                      "path": "M12 70 L88 70",
                      "color": "#C6C9FF"
                    },
                    {
                      "name": "Huyền",
                      "letter": "à",
                      "path": "M14 70 Q40 70 86 90",
                      "color": "#FFC6EF"
                    },
                    {
                      "name": "Hỏi",
                      "letter": "ả",
                      "path": "M12 88 C26 128 50 128 88 84",
                      "color": "#E6FFC6"
                    },
                    {
                      "name": "Ngã",
                      "letter": "ã",
                      "path": "M12 88 C26 128 50 128 88 84",
                      "color": "#C6FFF9"
                    },
                    {
                      "name": "Sắc",
                      "letter": "á",
                      "path": "M22 72 L78 10",
                      "color": "#FFC6C7"
                    },
                    {
                      "name": "Nặng",
                      "letter": "ạ",
                      "path": "M30 126 L70 136",
                      "color": "#FFFDC6"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "heading",
                  "text": "2. How to write tone marks in a word",
                  "tone": "purple"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "When writing tone marks in a word, make sure to put them on a vowel, not a consonant:"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "If there is only one vowel, the tone mark is put on that vowel."
                },
                {
                  "type": "wordChips",
                  "tone": "lav",
                  "items": [
                    "Đã",
                    "Mình",
                    "Bạn",
                    "Có",
                    "Cảm"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "If there are two or three vowels, but no consonant at the end, the tone mark is put on the second to last vowel."
                },
                {
                  "type": "wordChips",
                  "tone": "lav",
                  "items": [
                    "Hòa",
                    "Kiểu",
                    "Phải",
                    "Mỗi",
                    "Loại"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "If there are two or three vowels, and there is a consonant at the end, the tone mark is put on the last vowel."
                },
                {
                  "type": "wordChips",
                  "tone": "lav",
                  "items": [
                    "Tiếng",
                    "Việt",
                    "Nguyễn",
                    "Quỳnh"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "heading",
                  "text": "3. Importance of Tones and Tone Marks",
                  "tone": "purple"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "The use of tones is extremely important, as a different tone may cause the word to have an entirely new meaning. For example:"
                },
                {
                  "type": "table",
                  "columns": [
                    "Word",
                    "Meaning"
                  ],
                  "rows": [
                    [
                      "Ma",
                      "Ghost"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Mà",
                      "But"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Má",
                      "Mother / Cheek"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Mả",
                      "Grave"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Mã",
                      "Horse (Chinese origin), Appearance"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Mạ",
                      "Young rice stalk, Coating"
                    ]
                  ],
                  "sysFont": true
                }
              ]
            },
